ng on camera for the  first time in 10 days  u.s president donald trump lashed out at  congress over its just passed  coronavirus aid package  part of a 5500 page spending bill  the president calls a disgrace it's  called the coveted relief bill  but it has almost nothing to do with  covert this bill contains  85.5 million dollars for assistance to  cambodia 134 million dollars to burma  1.3 billion dollars for egypt but just  600  in aid for most americans i am asking  congress to amend this bill and increase  the  ridiculously low six hundred dollars  to two thousand dollars or four thousand  dollars  for a couple both democrats and  republicans bickered for months over a  second stimulus bill  even delaying their holiday break to  pass this one the bill is so massive  few if any lawmakers actually read it  republicans repeatedly blocked attempts  to give struggling americans more money  we do not have an unlimited checking  account the president's threat to  possibly veto the bill came just hours  after his own white house aides praised  the package  adding he would support it the president  has indicated his intent to sign the  bill  for a few reasons because this is going  to take care of american families with  stimulus checks  house speaker nancy pelosi says she's  ready to introduce a new bill this week  but she'll need the senate on board  to get people money they desperately  need i need to buy me some food  i don't have anything to buy some food  right now i'm running out of food stumps  if there's no agreement and the  president doesn't sign this bill  unemployment benefits for over 10  million americans  run out the day after christmas jennifer  johnson  global news washington trump is leaving  office but not without handing out  presidential pardons he's issued almost  30 pardons and commutations  they include his former campaign manager  paul manafort  charles kushner the father of trump's  son-in-law  john boltby and peter atkinson were also  pardoned  they were both convicted in a fraud  scheme involving lord conrad black  and two people convicted in the mueller  russia investigation  former campaign aide george papadopoulos  and lawyer alex  van der zwan both pleaded guilty to  lying to the fbi  twitter has decided to wipe millions of  followers from the official white house  accounts  when president trump leaves office next  month in 2016 trump of prolific tweeter  was automatically given barack obama's  existing followers  when his administration handed over the  twitter handles for the white house  which each had about 13 million  followers at the time  joe biden will be forced to start from  scratch twitter says followers will be  notified  and given a choice still ahead the crime  behind bars  and the prison guards facing charges  you're watching global national  more than a year after an indigenous man  was killed while in custody  charges have been laid jonathan hanukk  was in a prison in newfoundland and  labrador when he died  tonight a group of correctional officers  and prison guards is facing a range of  charges  ross lord reports the details of what  happened in this saint john's prison  more than a year ago are unclear  but what is known is disturbing inmate  jonathan hanouk  an indigenous man from labrador was  killed he was awaiting trial in the 2016  killing of an elderly woman  hanukkah had a big disadvantage in life  from the day he was born  he was suffering from fetal alcohol  spectrum disorder  he had a very difficult time with that  and our institutions here in  newfoundland had no  idea how to work with him and assist him  those charged in his death  are the same people whose job it is to  provide protection  police say they've laid charges against  10 correctional officers  their identities have not been released  three officers are charged with  manslaughter  one with the additional charge of  failure to provide the necessaries of  life  seven other prison guards are charged  with criminal negligence causing death  a police statement says the accused have  been released from custody  they're scheduled to appear in court in  february a lawyer for hanukk's family  questions why people charged with such  serious crimes  did not face a bail hearing something he  suggests is automatic for indigenous  suspects  and others the difference is that they  are correctional officers  and department of justice employees  that's the difference that's the  circumstance  that's the favoritism buckingham notes  chinook is the third inmate to die in  her majesty's penitentiary in the past  three years  he's calling for a public inquiry into  correctional policies  leadership and training for dealing with  mentally ill inmates  the province's justice minister has  issued a statement saying  we have and will continue to review  policies and procedures in adult  corrections  to ensure we meet best practices from  across the country  the statement sidesteps questions about  favoritism  and does not answer another question  whether the accused are still working at  the penitentiary  now that they've been charged in the  killing of someone in their custody  ross lord global news  up next sending hope a bc couple's  christmas wish for two canadians  held in china  christmas is all about being with loved  ones and it'll be tough this year for  most of us  but spare a thought for michael kovrick  and michael spavor the two canadians  detained in china  who are about to spend their third  christmas alone behind bars  a bc couple who were held for two years  in china  say even the smallest act of kindness  can make a world of difference  abigail beeman explains life in chinese  jail for kevin and julia garrett meant  interrogation  missed meals lights on 24 hours a day  your heads are you know yeah into the  aisle so there's people walking right  past your head  all night it's very very difficult  but through the excruciating ordeal  christmas was a fleeting moment of good  they did this beautiful act of kindness  a makeshift dinner was allowed one year  with their son the other with each other  then it just went back to the normal or  or worse than normal  and so i really feel for the two  michaels they'll be thinking of course a  family of christmas is past  and wanting the same thing again but  they won't be able to have it so  i'm praying and hoping that they at  least the government will allow them to  have a call or something with their  family julia was behind bars for six  months then on house arrest in china  kevin was imprisoned for 775 days  michael kovrig and michael spavor will  soon reach that milestone  they're now facing their third christmas  behind bars  the garretts see the two cases as  similar they were expats in china for 30  years near the north korean border  they were picked up by chinese state  security in 2014  after canada detained chinese citizen su  bin in vancouver  wanted for extradition by the u.s much  like mangwon joe  except the garretts point out the stakes  are higher with a huawei executive vip  the government at the beginning had  indicated to our family  that nothing ever resolves within two  years the garretts encourage everyone to  advocate for kovrig and spavor and join  in the christmas card writing campaign  to chinese embassies  it doesn't matter if they ever see the  card they hear that the cards are there  stacked up piled up and they think okay  people care they're still behind the  scenes fighting that  to me is kind of helped me get through  all those  long lonely moments they'll hear about  the cards  say the garretts from consular visits  supposed to happen once a month coverg  and spavor didn't have them for months  during the pandemic  but have had three in the past three  months those 30 minutes were life-giving  because i got messages from julia from  my family from our kids  they also at some point later on let us  we have photos of my family  eventually the garrett's had a happy  ending kevin was put on a plane home  with little warning  and the family was reunited at the  vancouver airport a resolution they  believe possible for the two canadians  too their family waiting for them inside  the door  and that door will open and they will  just walk through and there will be this  amazing  reunion hug that will it changed our  lives they will never  forget that joyful moment global affairs  won't say whether canada's ambassador  has told the two men about all the  christmas cards  nor whether china has made any guarantee  that the visits will continue  a spokesperson will only say canada  works tirelessly  for meaningful and ongoing access  abigail beeman global news  ottawa and that is global national for  this wednesday night  i'm robin gill tonight your canada is  port elgin ontario we would love to see  your corner of this country so please  keep sending your photos to viewers at  globalnational.com  thank you for watching and i'll see you  back here tomorrow have a great night  you
 

